ui Water Displays  Water is a very powerful element in Feng Shui. Therefore, if you have decided to get a Water Display because you like it, here are some guidelines that you should keep in mind:  The shape and what it represents:  In this case, you should pay close attention to the room where you want to place it and if that font makes sense with the rest of the decorative objects.  Sound:  Once you have chosen your ideal Glass wall fountain, now you have to consider the sound of the water falling. Do you like it? Find a sound that pleases you and relaxes you. Of course, you also have to take into account the engine noise. It often happens that, in small Custom Water Walls, the sound of the motor is louder than that of the water jump. This you should avoid. Find some Feng Shui Water Displays with which you can only hear the relaxing noise of the waterfall.  The size:  You must follow your intuition again since no size is the most recommended, but it is a matter of taste and the place where you want to place it.  Outdoor Water Displays will always be larger than an indoor one, and the sound of falling water will also be louder. Inside, for space, the Feng Shui water fountain will be smaller, logically. But we encourage you not to be conditioned by this.",
